# CPR$ — Code, Proof, Review Costs

A small accounting framework for the dollar cost of producing verified
software with AI-paired tooling. Three numbers and one ratio tell the
story:

| # | Symbol | Name           | What it measures                                                                |
|--:|:-------|:---------------|:--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| 1 | C      | Cost of Code   | Dollar cost of producing the executable code (with or without verification).    |
| 2 | P      | Cost of Proof  | Dollar cost of producing the specifications, contracts, and proofs that verify the code. |
| 3 | R      | Review Ratio   | Fraction of the verified deliverable that the proofgrammer must read by hand. Trustable lines (LOC0R) are excluded from the numerator. |
| 4 | C+P    | Total          | The full bill for the verified artifact.                                        |

CPR$ deliberately does not collapse C and P into one number. The two
costs scale very differently with project size, problem domain, and
proof tooling, and most engineering decisions hinge on which is bigger.

## Inputs

CPR$ is computed from the output of two veracity tools, plus four
externally-tracked numbers:

| # | Input                          | Source                                         | Used for |
|--:|:-------------------------------|:-----------------------------------------------|:---------|
| 1 | LOC, LoEC, LoPTT counts        | `veracity-count-loc`                           | C, P, R denominators |
| 2 | LOPC2R, LOC0R, LoEC by category| `veracity-count-lines-of-review`               | C/P split, R |
| 3 | `--programmer-costs` ($ / yr)  | external (HR)                                  | hourly programmer rate |
| 4 | `--ai-costs` ($ / yr)          | external (real spend, see "AI costs" below)    | hourly AI rate |
| 5 | `--person-days`                | external (git log committed-days)              | task-hours |
| 6 | `--average-hours-per-day`      | external (git commit-interval avg)             | task-hours |

Fixed constants: 220 work days / year, 8 hours / day → 1,760 hours / year.

## How to compute C, P, and R

### Per-project totals

```
hourly_programmer = programmer_costs / 1,760
hourly_AI         = ai_costs         / 1,760
total_hours       = person_days × average_hours_per_day
programmer_cost   = total_hours × hourly_programmer
AI_cost           = total_hours × hourly_AI
total_cost        = programmer_cost + AI_cost
```

### Splitting total_cost into C and P

For a project that contains both code and verification (Verus): apportion
by line-class share. The "code share" is the LoEC fraction of total LOC.

```
LoEC_share         = LoEC / (LoEC + LoLC + LOP + Spec + LODT + FnTySig + FnContract + LoAA + LoPTT)
C_project          = total_cost × LoEC_share
P_project          = total_cost × (1 − LoEC_share)
```

For a project that contains only code (no verification): C = total_cost,
P = 0.

### Combining multiple projects

If the verified deliverable is the result of two efforts (e.g.,
unverified prototype followed by a verified rewrite), sum the per-project
C and P:

```
C_combined = Σ C_project
P_combined = Σ P_project
```

The ratio R is computed once on the **deliverable**, not on the sum:

```
R = LOPC2R / (LOPC2R + LOC0R)         on the verified deliverable
```

LOC from a discarded prototype does not appear in R because the
proofgrammer does not review what isn't shipped.

## AI costs — split actual spend, don't trust the rate

The `--ai-costs` flag wants a yearly amortized rate. In practice the
right number to give it is **derived from actual receipts**, not from a
plan-list price. To convert real spend back into a yearly rate:

```
hourly_AI       = total_AI_spend / total_task_hours
ai_costs_input  = hourly_AI × 1,760
```

Apply the same `--ai-costs` value to every invocation that participated
in the same spending bucket. The `total_hours × hourly_AI` formula then
distributes the spend proportional to task-hours across the projects.

Three plausible split methods if you have multiple projects on one
subscription:

| # | Method                | When to prefer |
|--:|:----------------------|:---------------|
| 1 | Task-hours (default)  | Cleanest. Same denominator the cost math already uses. Yields a single shared `--ai-costs` value. |
| 2 | Committed-days        | If AI usage was roughly steady-state per active day across projects. |
| 3 | Output-line-count     | If AI usage tracked output volume (rare). |
| 4 | User judgment         | Use only if you have a clear sense of where the spend went, e.g. "90 % was on the Verus project". |

## Worked example — APAS-AI + Rusticate + APAS-VERUS + Veracity

### Honest framing

- APAS-AI started with specs in hand (algorithm specs from APAS textbook).
- APAS-VERUS started with both specs and code from APAS-AI.
- APAS-VERUS rewrote almost all of APAS-AI's code in Verus style (typeclass-impl pattern, `spec_*_wf` predicates). What transferred was design intent and algorithm choice, not concrete code.

### Inputs

| # | Project                  | Person-days | Avg hrs/day | Hours    | LOC     | LoEC   | LOPC2R | LOC0R  |
|--:|:-------------------------|------------:|------------:|---------:|--------:|-------:|-------:|-------:|
| 1 | APAS-AI + Rusticate      | 60          | 5.16        | 309.60   | 31,751  | 31,751 | —      | —      |
| 2 | APAS-VERUS + Veracity    | 119         | 9.44        | 1,123.36 | 166,401 | 56,549 | 47,828 | 95,908 |
| 3 | Combined                 | 179         | —           | 1,432.96 |         |        |        |        |

### Cost rates

| # | Quantity                  | Value          | Notes |
|--:|:--------------------------|---------------:|:------|
| 1 | `--programmer-costs`      | $ 375,000 / yr | Senior + 50 % loading (taxes, benefits, overhead) |
| 2 | Actual AI spend (total)   | ≤ $ 7,000      | Real receipts since APAS-AI started |
| 3 | Hourly AI from spend      | $ 4.886 / hr   | $ 7,000 / 1,432.96 hrs |
| 4 | `--ai-costs` (annualized) | **$ 8,599 / yr** | $ 4.886 × 1,760 |

### Split AI spend by task-hours

| # | Project               | Hours share | AI $    |
|--:|:----------------------|------------:|--------:|
| 1 | APAS-AI + Rusticate   | 21.6 %      | $ 1,512 |
| 2 | APAS-VERUS + Veracity | 78.4 %      | $ 5,488 |
| 3 | Total                 | 100  %      | $ 7,000 |

### Per-project totals (with `--ai-costs 8599`)

| # | Quantity       | APAS-AI + Rusticate | APAS-VERUS + Veracity |
|--:|:---------------|--------------------:|----------------------:|
| 1 | Programmer cost | $  65,965           | $ 239,352             |
| 2 | AI cost        | $   1,512           | $   5,488             |
| 3 | **Total cost** | **$  67,477**       | **$ 244,840**         |
| 4 | AI share       |  2.2 %              |  2.2 %                |

### CPR$ — combined

Apportioning APAS-VERUS by line-class share. LoEC share = 56,549 / 166,401 = **34.0 %**.

| # | Quantity                                          | Calculation                                | Value           |
|--:|:--------------------------------------------------|:-------------------------------------------|----------------:|
| 1 | C₁ — APAS-AI all-code portion                     | (all of APAS-AI total)                     | $   67,477      |
| 2 | C₂ — APAS-VERUS code-rewrite portion              | 0.340 × $ 244,840                          | $   83,246      |
| 3 | **C — Cost of Code (combined)**                   | C₁ + C₂                                    | **$  150,723**  |
| 4 | P₁ — APAS-AI                                      | 0 (no proof)                               | $        0      |
| 5 | P₂ — APAS-VERUS proof + spec portion              | $ 244,840 − $ 83,246                       | $  161,594      |
| 6 | **P — Cost of Proof (combined)**                  | P₁ + P₂                                    | **$  161,594**  |
| 7 | **C + P**                                         | sum                                        | **$  312,317**  |
| 8 | **R — Review Ratio**                              | LOPC2R / (LOPC2R + LOC0R) on the deliverable | **0.333 (33.3 %)** |

### Per-line readings

| # | Quantity                                       | Calculation        | Value      |
|--:|:-----------------------------------------------|:-------------------|-----------:|
| 1 | $ / verified deliverable line (LOC = 166,401)  | 312,317 / 166,401  | $ 1.877    |
| 2 | C / LoEC (combined)                            | 150,723 /  56,549  | $ 2.665    |
| 3 | P / LOPC2R                                     | 161,594 /  47,828  | $ 3.378    |
| 4 | P / LOP                                        | 161,594 /  25,627  | $ 6.305    |

### Honest disclaimer (for emails / reports)

> The combined figure $312,317 includes the APAS-AI prototype that
> APAS-VERUS subsequently rewrote in Verus style. Code lineage is partial:
> design and algorithm choice carried over from APAS-AI, but most concrete
> code did not. AI cost is split by task-hours across the two projects,
> totaling ≤ $ 7,000 of real spend. The CPR$ split (C $ 150,723 / P $ 161,594 / R 33.3 %)
> attributes APAS-VERUS proportionally by line-class share; alternative
> attributions are possible.

## Comparison anchor — seL4 (2009)

seL4 is the canonical pre-AI Verus-equivalent point in the cost space.
Numbers below use NICTA / Data61 published estimates and a 40-hour work
week (2,080 hrs / yr). Volumes in K-units (KLOE = thousand lines of
executable code; KLOP = thousand lines of proof + spec).

| # | Quantity                     | seL4            | Notes                                              |
|--:|:-----------------------------|----------------:|:---------------------------------------------------|
| 1 | Person-years                 |            22.5 |                                                    |
| 2 | Hours                        |          46,800 | 22.5 × 2,080                                       |
| 3 | KLOE                         |              10 | C source — 10,000 LOE                              |
| 4 | KLOP                         |             480 | Isabelle/HOL spec + proof — 480,000 LOP            |
| 5 | KLOP / KLOE ratio            |              48 | 48 lines of proof per line of executable code      |
| 6 | Programmer cost              |    $ 8,437,500  | 22.5 × $ 375,000 — programmer-only, no AI          |
| 7 | AI cost                      |    $          0 | Pre-LLM era; Isabelle/HOL tactics are not AI cost  |
| 8 | **C + P (total)**            | **$ 8,437,500** |                                                    |
| 9 | $ / KLine                    |       $ 17,219  | $ 8,437,500 / 490 KLines                           |
| 10| $ / KLOE                     |      $ 843,750  | $ 8,437,500 / 10 KLOE                              |
| 11| $ / KLOP                     |       $ 17,578  | $ 8,437,500 / 480 KLOP                             |

### Head-to-head — seL4 vs APAS-VERUS + Veracity

For APAS-VERUS, KLOE and KLOP analogues are computed from the line
classifier:
- **KLOE** = LoEC (executable Verus bodies) ≈ 56.5
- **KLOP** = everything else in the verified deliverable
  (LOC0R − LoEC + LOPC2R contracts/specs + LoPTT) ≈ 110

(Excluding LoAA and LoRTT/LoBT.)

| # | Quantity              | seL4 (pre-AI) | APAS-VERUS + Veracity (AI-paired) | Ratio        |
|--:|:----------------------|--------------:|----------------------------------:|:-------------|
| 1 | Person-years          |        22.5   |              0.64                 | seL4  ~35 ×  |
| 2 | Hours                 |      46,800   |              1,123                | seL4  ~42 ×  |
| 3 | KLOE                  |          10   |              ~ 57                 | Verus ~5.7 × |
| 4 | KLOP                  |         480   |             ~ 110                 | seL4  ~4.4 × |
| 5 | KLOP / KLOE           |          48   |              ~ 1.9                | seL4  ~25 ×  (proof bloat) |
| 6 | Total Klines          |         490   |             ~ 167                 | seL4  ~2.9 × |
| 7 | Klines / hour         |       0.0105  |              0.148                | Verus ~14 ×  |
| 8 | $ / KLine             |    $ 17,219   |          ~ $ 1,471 \*             | seL4  ~11.7 ×|
| 9 | $ / KLOE              |   $ 843,750   |          ~ $ 4,300 \*             | seL4  ~196 × |
| 10| $ / KLOP              |    $ 17,578   |          ~ $ 2,225 \*             | seL4  ~7.9 × |
| 11| C + P total           | $ 8,437,500   |          $ 244,840 \*             | seL4  ~34.5 ×|

\* using `--ai-costs 8599` (real-spend rate) — replaces the earlier $90,000 placeholder.

The most striking row is **5**: Verus needs only ~ 1.9 lines of proof
per line of executable, vs. seL4's 48. SMT automation does most of the
heavy lifting; Isabelle/HOL needed everything tactic-spelled.

### Caveats

| # | Caveat |
|--:|:-------|
| 1 | Different problem domain: seL4 verified a concurrent kernel with refinement / memory-safety proofs; APAS-VERUS verifies textbook algorithms. Kernel proofs are harder per line. |
| 2 | Different proof assistants: Isabelle/HOL (tactic-heavy) vs Verus (SMT-backed, more automation even without AI). |
| 3 | AI usage is a **lower bound** — the 1,123-hour task-hour figure undercounts background proof runs that occurred while the proofgrammer was away. Actual AI cost is bounded above by total-spend receipts. |
| 4 | seL4's hours figure includes design, review, documentation, integration with the rest of the OS; APAS-VERUS hours are largely proof engineering. |

Even after the caveats, the order-of-magnitude signal stands: AI-paired
Verus is producing verified code at roughly an order of magnitude less
human time per line than Isabelle/HOL was producing it in 2009.

## Tool support — `veracity-count-loc`

`veracity-count-loc` emits the cost-analysis block when these flags are
set together (validated; missing or extra produces an error):

| # | Flag                          | Required when                      |
|--:|:------------------------------|:-----------------------------------|
| 1 | `--programmer-costs`          | cost mode                          |
| 2 | `--ai-costs`                  | cost mode                          |
| 3 | `--person-days`               | cost mode                          |
| 4 | `--average-hours-per-day`     | cost mode                          |
| 5 | `--ai-paired-programming`     | exclusive of (6); enables cost mode |
| 6 | `--ai-paired-proving`         | exclusive of (5); enables cost mode |
| 7 | `--projects`                  | optional (label only)              |

For proving mode, `veracity-count-loc` invokes the sibling
`veracity-count-lines-of-review` binary to fetch LOPC2R / LOC0R / LoPTT
totals and reports `$ / LOC`, `$ / LOPC2R`, `$ / LOC0R`. For programming
mode, only `$ / LOC` is reported.

The cost block is appended to the regular per-file and per-chapter
tables in `analyses/veracity-count-loc.YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.log`.
